**Day 31–40: Introduction to NoSQL with MongoDB**  

**Topic:**  
Introduction to NoSQL databases, focusing on MongoDB, including its architecture, document-based storage, and querying methods.  

**Learning Objectives:**  

• Understand NoSQL concepts and differences from relational databases.  
• Learn MongoDB document structure and CRUD operations.  
• Explore indexing, aggregation, and performance optimization in MongoDB.  

**Activities / Deliverables:**  

• Set up MongoDB locally and perform basic CRUD operations.  
• Design a document schema for a sample application.  
• Implement aggregation pipelines for data analysis.  

**Important Concepts:**  

• Document-oriented database  
• BSON (Binary JSON) format  
• Sharding and replication  

**SQL Syntax / Commands:**  

• `db.collection.insertOne()`  
• `db.collection.aggregate()`  
• `db.collection.createIndex()`  

**Real-world Use Cases:**  

• Storing user profiles with flexible schemas.  
• Real-time analytics using aggregation pipelines.  

**Tools / Tech:**  

• MongoDB Compass  
• MongoDB Atlas (Cloud)  

**Summary:**  
Learned NoSQL fundamentals, MongoDB operations, and real-world applications for scalable data storage.  

